-- entity_container_degree: how many higher-tier laplace.entities contain each id.
--
-- This is inverse-document-frequency derived from the substrate's own structure
-- rather than from a word list. A token that appears inside almost every
-- trajectory carries almost no information about which trajectory you meant; a
-- token that appears inside sixteen of them carries a great deal. That is true
-- in any language and any modality, because containment is a property of the
-- composition hierarchy, not of English.
--
-- MEASURED 2026-08-04 on the foundation ladder (1-hop, cap 20000):
--     a 20000+ | the 20000+ | of 20000+ | water 4629 | hot 1040
--     glacier 83 | pawn 23 | france 16
-- The separation is total and needs no stop list. Compare the alternatives that
-- were measured and REJECTED on the same set:
--   * highway popcount  — 'a' scores 19, the HIGHEST in the set, because the
--     tier-0 floor participates in every band. Degree, not specificity.
--   * total_mass        — elects 'chess' over 'pawn'; rewards volume.
--   * ord DESC          — an SVO word-order prior. Wrong for SOV, VSO, a chess
--     position, or an image, in a substrate that is modality-agnostic.
--
-- p_cap is a symptom, not a dial to retune. structural.containers_of ENUMERATES
-- rows to produce a COUNT, so every cap trades separation against latency: a cap
-- low enough to be fast reports the same degree for an ordinary content word as
-- for a pure function word, and a cap high enough to separate them puts a
-- multi-second call under converse.resolve — converse.election_token_profile and
-- prompt_coherence.c:351 both call this on the resolve path. The fix is a
-- maintained or index-only count that never materialises the container rows.
--
-- icf is a PER-TOKEN SCALAR. INVENTION §7 forbids deciding a ranking on one, and
-- #861 requires a key combining what the fold produces per edge. This is an input
-- to an election, never the election.
--
-- Set-based over the whole id array in one call: per-row resolution of this is
-- the read-path defect the architecture rules name explicitly.
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS laplace.entity_container_degree(bytea[], integer);
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION structural.entity_container_degree(
    p_ids bytea[],
    p_cap integer DEFAULT 8192)
    RETURNS TABLE(entity_id bytea, degree bigint, icf double precision)
    LANGUAGE sql STABLE PARALLEL SAFE AS $$
    SELECT t.id,
           count(c.entity_id)::bigint,
           /* 1 / log2(2 + degree): 1.0 for an id nothing contains, ~0.077 at a
            * cap of 8192. Monotone decreasing, never zero, so it orders cleanly
            * as a ranking key and never annihilates a product.
            *
            * ln()/ln(2) rather than log(base, x): the two-argument log() is
            * numeric-only, so the double-precision form does not resolve and
            * casting through numeric would cost a conversion per group for a
            * value that is only ever compared. */
           (ln(2.0) / ln(2.0 + count(c.entity_id)::double precision))::double precision
    FROM unnest(p_ids) AS t(id)
    LEFT JOIN LATERAL structural.containers_of(t.id, 1, p_cap) c ON true
    GROUP BY t.id
$$;
